<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aristomenes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aristomenes is the legendary hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messenians">Messenians</a>, said to have led their revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-messenian-war">Second Messenian War</a> in the 7th century BCE. According to the account preserved by Pausanias, he won early victories, held out for years in the mountain stronghold of Eira and escaped capture several times before the Messenians were defeated. After the refoundation of Messene in 369 BCE he was honoured there with a hero cult.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aristomenes.jpg" alt="Aristomenes" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edmund Ollier Publication date 1882 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aristomenes_fighting_his_way_out_of_Ira.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
